  "code_findings": [
    "Every local move perturbs all continuous route coordinates; the entire flight is replayed for each candidate.",
    "Local geometry is built around a fixed, limited set of guide centres; mode changes are not paired with a compensating control-target update.",
    "Independent command slots include redundant permutations of the same physical command sequence, whereas encoded guide centres order each command kind by time. This is avoidable computational redundancy, not proof of a wrong prior or the sole failure cause.",
    "A zero likelihood outside hard physical/fuel support becomes zero at every positive tempering exponent. The observed first exponent of 1e-10 does not make that support restriction gradual.",
    "Finite-run geographical disagreement establishes failure to obtain a stable estimate. Acceptance or ancestral counts alone cannot establish convergence or identify every cause."
  ],
  "candidate_corrections_not_yet_validated": [
    "Use ordered event times with the correct order-statistic density and retain the intended physical prior.",
    "Construct observation-guided updates of shorter trajectory segments with full proposal-density correction; update categorical modes and continuous controls jointly.",
    "Retain revisability of earlier flight segments and useful distinct route families, and handle near-deterministic dynamics explicitly.",
    "Measure and reduce full replay overhead by reusing unchanged prefix state and sufficient statistics when exact.",
    "Validate on an independently calculable constrained reference, flexible noisy synthetic data, and withheld known-flight data with independent seeds before scaling."
  ],
